    "musical_direction": "Approx 25.7 seconds plus release. Arena-rock fart fanfare: firm bright pitched lead with clean sustained note bodies, alternating articulations only at phrase boundaries; double selected long notes a quiet octave down, then add a second slightly nasal lead for the second hook. Use deep round fart bass on roots/fifths, syncopated chord stabs at low volume, dry short plop kick, papery clap/snare fart, tiny squeaks as hats, and a playful rising fill in the turnaround. Preserve the 1/16+1/16+quarter attack cells, ties and silence before each answering figure; do not fill every melodic gap with loud effects. Because the first 1.5 beats of score rest were cut, original score barlines are at 2.5, 6.5, 10.5, ...; drum accents can align to that grid, with the first phrase unaccompanied or lightly accented until 2.5. Build the second hook wider and fuller, then thin out under the long dominant C#5 and land a big F#4 + low F# chord final fart at 46.5 beats."
  },
